---
description: Rules for the public website and screening app
globs: web/**, site/**, app/build.py, netlify.toml
alwaysApply: false
---
- Edit web/parts/*.html, never the built files in site/; run `python app/build.py` to regenerate. site/ is the Netlify publish directory and holds built output only (index.html, 404.html).
- Every published page is a single self-contained file. Only Google Fonts may load from the network. No analytics, trackers, remote images or CDNs. netlify.toml's Content-Security-Policy is the enforced version of that rule; widen it only with a reason.
- Design tokens (keep them): fog #EEF2F0, panel #E2EAE7, ink #0E2A33, muted #3D5E52, tide #1D6B74 (interactive), heat #A8650A (heat quantities and cautions only), line #C3D2CD; dark-mode equivalents are in web/parts/1_head.html. Fonts: Public Sans for UI and headings, Source Serif 4 for reading text and clauses.
- heat #A8650A is 4.1:1 on the light background, so it may only be used for text at 18.66 px bold or larger. Small heat-coloured text uses --heat-text (#8A5308, 5.6:1); in dark mode --heat-text equals --heat. Do not put --heat back on small text to "match the palette": axe-core will fail the build.
- Avoid: all-caps eyebrow labels, arrows on buttons, identical shadowed cards, gradient washes, decorative numbering on non-sequences.
- Accessibility: WCAG 2.2 AA, visible focus, labels on every input, results announced with aria-live, colour never the only signal, prefers-reduced-motion respected.
- Must work at 390 px wide, in dark mode, and with no horizontal page scroll; wide tables scroll inside `.scroll`.
- Copy is plain, specific and in sentence case. Errors say what went wrong and how to fix it.
- Every number the app shows comes from app/engine.js; no hard-coded results in markup except the hero defaults.
- tests/test_site.py (marker `site`) drives site/index.html in Chromium and runs axe-core from the local node_modules copy. Serious or critical violations fail. Run `pip install -e ".[site]" && python -m playwright install chromium && npm install` first.
